<template>
    <SiteShell page="home">
        <section class="hero">
            <div class="hero__copy">
                <span class="tag">2.5-axis · deterministic · unreleased</span>
                <h1>
                    Toolpaths and G-code<br />
                    that reproduce from plain text.
                </h1>
                <p class="hero__sub">
                    OpenCAM keeps one rectangular stock, a tool table and a list
                    of operations in a single <code>.ocam</code> document. A Rust
                    session owns validation, toolpath generation and the program;
                    the CLI, Node-API addon and TypeScript SDK are wrappers over
                    that same core. Unimplemented routes return
                    <code>capability/not-implemented</code> instead of an
                    approximation.
                </p>

                <dl class="spec">
                    <div class="spec__row">
                        <dt>Strategies</dt>
                        <dd>face · contour · pocket · drill</dd>
                    </div>
                    <div class="spec__row">
                        <dt>Depth control</dt>
                        <dd>multi-pass stepdown · raster stepover</dd>
                    </div>
                    <div class="spec__row">
                        <dt>Units</dt>
                        <dd>mm · mm/min · rpm, no conversion</dd>
                    </div>
                    <div class="spec__row">
                        <dt>Output</dt>
                        <dd>G-code · JSON · CSV · Markdown</dd>
                    </div>
                </dl>

                <div class="hero__cta">
                    <Link to="FeaturesPage" class="btn btn--primary">
                        Open feature index
                    </Link>
                    <Link to="RoadmapPage" class="btn btn--ghost">
                        Read the gate log
                    </Link>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="sheet" aria-hidden="true">
                <div class="sheet__head">
                    <span class="sheet__no">SHEET 01 / 03</span>
                    <span>FACE · CONTOUR · DRILL</span>
                    <span class="sheet__rev">REV 0</span>
                </div>

                <div class="draw">
                    <div class="draw__canvas">
                        <span class="stock"></span>
                        <i class="raster" v-for="row in rasterRows" :key="row" :style="{ top: row + 'px' }"></i>
                        <span class="hole" style="left: 44px; top: 40px"></span>
                        <span class="hole" style="left: 212px; top: 96px"></span>
                        <span class="hole" style="left: 128px; top: 132px"></span>
                        <span class="dim" style="left: 20px; top: 174px; width: 240px"></span>
                        <span class="dim__tick" style="left: 20px; top: 170px"></span>
                        <span class="dim__tick" style="left: 260px; top: 170px"></span>
                        <span class="dim-label">120 mm</span>
                        <span class="note">6 mm flat · S12000 · F1200</span>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="readout">
                    <div class="readout__row">
                        <span>moves</span>
                        <b>{{ moves }}</b>
                        <i>segments</i>
                    </div>
                    <div class="readout__row">
                        <span>cut length</span>
                        <b>{{ cutLength }}</b>
                        <i>mm</i>
                    </div>
                    <div class="readout__row">
                        <span>cycle time</span>
                        <b>{{ cycleTime }}</b>
                        <i>s</i>
                    </div>
                    <div class="readout__row readout__row--ok">
                        <span>validation</span>
                        <b>PASS</b>
                        <i>ok: true</i>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="sheet__foot">
                    <span>$ open-cam gcode bracket.ocam --out bracket.nc</span>
                    <span>exit 0</span>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="section-head">
                <h2><span class="section-index">01</span>Capability matrix</h2>
                <p>What this build actually generates, and what fails with a stable error code.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="table-wrap">
                <table class="matrix">
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th>Code</th>
                            <th>Capability</th>
                            <th>Method</th>
                            <th>Status</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr v-for="row in capabilityRows" :key="row.code">
                            <td class="name">{{ row.code }}</td>
                            <td>{{ row.capability }}</td>
                            <td class="method">{{ row.method }}</td>
                            <td><span :class="statusChip(row.status)">{{ row.status }}</span></td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
            <p class="table-note">
                The machine-readable matrix is printed by
                <code>open-cam capabilities</code> and matches actual behaviour at
                every entry point.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="section-head">
                <h2><span class="section-index">02</span>One core, four surfaces</h2>
                <p>No toolpath rule is reimplemented in a binding.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="table-wrap">
                <table class="matrix">
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th>Surface</th>
                            <th>Package</th>
                            <th>Responsibility</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="name">Rust session</td>
                            <td class="name">cam-model</td>
                            <td>Document I/O, editing, validation, toolpaths, G-code and reports.</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="name">Node-API</td>
                            <td class="name">cam-napi</td>
                            <td>Orthogonal functions over the session; each returns JSON.</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="name">TypeScript SDK</td>
                            <td class="name">@wae/open-cam</td>
                            <td><code>new OpenCAM()</code> session, <code>CamDocument</code> documents, atomic save.</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="name">CLI</td>
                            <td class="name">open-cam</td>
                            <td>Argument parsing, JSON output and exit codes <code>0</code> / <code>1</code> / <code>2</code> only.</td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="section-head">
                <h2><span class="section-index">03</span>Workflow</h2>
                <p>Declare, validate, generate, export. Every edit writes the document atomically.</p>
            </div>
            <ol class="flow">
                <li class="flow-step">
                    <span class="flow-index">01</span>
                    <h3>Declare</h3>
                    <p>Create an <code>.ocam</code> file with a stock, tools and operations.</p>
                    <span class="chip chip--available">available</span>
                </li>
                <li class="flow-step">
                    <span class="flow-index">02</span>
                    <h3>Validate</h3>
                    <p>Check tool geometry, depth, stepover and every hole against the stock.</p>
                    <span class="chip chip--available">available</span>
                </li>
                <li class="flow-step">
                    <span class="flow-index">03</span>
                    <h3>Generate</h3>
                    <p>Expand each operation into rapid, plunge and cut moves with metrics.</p>
                    <span class="chip chip--available">available</span>
                </li>
                <li class="flow-step">
                    <span class="flow-index">04</span>
                    <h3>Export</h3>
                    <p>Write G-code, JSON, CSV or a Markdown report through one atomic writer.</p>
                    <span class="chip chip--available">available</span>
                </li>
            </ol>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="section-head">
                <h2><span class="section-index">04</span>Deterministic by construction</h2>
                <p>No timestamps, no randomised ordering, no machine-specific output.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="table-wrap">
                <table class="matrix">
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th>Rule</th>
                            <th>Consequence</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="name">level_depths</td>
                            <td class="method">passes end exactly at the requested depth</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="name">line_positions</td>
                            <td class="method">rasters always cut both stock edges</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="name">cutter radius</td>
                            <td class="method">contours offset outward, pockets shrink inward</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="name">post</td>
                            <td class="method">generic absolute millimetre mill, <code>G81</code>/<code>G83</code> cycles</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td class="name">reports</td>
                            <td class="method">byte-identical on repeated runs</td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="section-head">
                <h2><span class="section-index">05</span>Scope</h2>
                <p>A narrow CAM kernel with an explicit boundary.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="grid-2">
                <article class="card scope-card scope-card--in">
                    <span class="chip chip--available">in scope</span>
                    <h3>Implemented today</h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Rectangular stock in millimetres</li>
                        <li>Tool table with spindle and cutting/plunge feeds</li>
                        <li>Raster facing of the stock top</li>
                        <li>Outside rectangular profiling with cutter-radius offset</li>
                        <li>Rectangular pocket clearing with raster lines</li>
                        <li>Drilling with <code>G81</code> and peck <code>G83</code></li>
                        <li>Multi-pass Z depth and configurable stepover</li>
                        <li>Toolpath metrics and cycle-time estimate</li>
                        <li>G-code, JSON, CSV and Markdown export</li>
                    </ul>
                </article>
                <article class="card scope-card scope-card--out">
                    <span class="chip chip--blocked">out of scope</span>
                    <h3>Rejected, not approximated</h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li>3D surfacing and STL/solid input</li>
                        <li>Adaptive or trochoidal clearing</li>
                        <li>Turning and mill-turn</li>
                        <li>Four-axis and five-axis work</li>
                        <li>STEP and DXF import</li>
                        <li>Vendor post-processors</li>
                        <li>Graphical toolpath viewport</li>
                    </ul>
                </article>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="status-band">
            <div>
                <span class="eyebrow">Build status</span>
                <h2>The kernel is real. The interface is the terminal.</h2>
                <p>
                    Create, edit, validate, generate and export a job today. Read
                    the toolpath report to check every move, then run the program
                    or inspect the Markdown summary. Each unimplemented route
                    fails with <code>capability/not-implemented</code> and exit
                    code <code>2</code>.
                </p>
            </div>
            <Link to="RoadmapPage" class="btn btn--ghost">Read the gate log</Link>
        </section>

        <p class="cta-line">
            Want the detailed surface?
            <Link to="FeaturesPage">Read the feature index</Link>
            .
        </p>
    </SiteShell>
</template>

<style>
.hero {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.06fr 0.94fr;
